   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I used this package to run the 7-day PA data. </div><div>The summary file report only shows the time in MVPA but no LPA, MPA, VPA, and sedentary time. I looked up the Part 5 summary file found the variables:</div><div><br></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#888888\">sleep duration = dur_nightsleep_min <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#888888\">sedentary time = dur_TINday_min<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#888888\">LPA time = dur_TLIGday_min<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#888888\">MPA time = dur_TMODday_min <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#888888\">VPA time = dur_TVIGday_min<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#888888\">Total wear time = dur_nightandday_min<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#888888\">Non-wear time = nonwear_hours<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><br></div><div>To me understanding, this should be the average daily LPA, MPA, VPA, MVPA. But it turns out there is a huge difference between the GGIR file report and the Part 5 variables. Can anyone help me with this issue? should I divide by 7 days for those variables?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tCq0DcmFAQAJ",
   "from": "Vincent van Hees",
   "author": "13568954e9b4ef4b",
   "date": "2020-04-09T14:15:21Z",
   "subject": "Re: [GGIR] Regarding the MVPA result",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>What variables from which files are you comparing? I cannot follow your question.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Vignette paragraph 4.3 <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/GGIR/vignettes/GGIR.html#output-part-5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/GGIR/vignettes/GGIR.html%23output-part-5&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792490875885000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Oppt0BjGE48VSLnbXKEJM\">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/GGIR/vignettes/GGIR.html#output-part-5</a>  gives guidance for variable meanings.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Note that sedentary behavior is not calculated by GGIR. GGIR only gives inactive behavior split up in sustained inactivity and other inactivity. It is up to you to call this sedentary behaviour, but given that we do not estimate sitting time it wouldn&#39;t sound logical to me to call it sedentary behavior.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Vincent</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>‐‐‐‐‐‐‐ Original Message ‐‐‐‐‐‐‐<br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div> On Tuesday, April 7, 2020 5:42 AM, woodstock78 &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">liuwenx...@hotmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><div> <br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello,<br></div><div><br></div><div>I used this package to run the 7-day PA data. <br></div><div>The summary file report only shows the time in MVPA but no LPA, MPA, VPA, and sedentary time. I looked up the Part 5 summary file found the variables:<br></div><div><br></div><div><p align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">sleep duration = dur_nightsleep_min </span></span></span><br></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">sedentary time = dur_TINday_min</span></span></span><br></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">LPA time = dur_TLIGday_min</span></span></span><br></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">MPA time = dur_TMODday_min </span></span></span><br></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">VPA time = dur_TVIGday_min</span></span></span><br></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">Total wear time = dur_nightandday_min</span></span></span><br></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">Non-wear time = nonwear_hours</span></span></span><br></p></div><div><br></div><div>To me understanding, this should be the average daily LPA, MPA, VPA, MVPA. But it turns out there is a huge difference between the GGIR file report and the Part 5 variables. Can anyone help me with this issue? should I divide by 7 days for those variables?<br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!<br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><p><br></p></blockquote>"
