     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello Vincent,<div><br></div><div>Thanks for your reply. Let me rephrase my question. I intended to use these variables (<span style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136);font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">LPA time = dur_TLIGday_min; </span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136);font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">MPA time = dur_TMODday_min ; </span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136);font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">VPA time = dur_TVIGday_min</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"><font color=\"#000000\">) to calculate the light PA, Moderate PA, and Vigorous PA. When I add variables (</font></span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136);font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13.3333px\">dur_TMODday_min and </span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136);font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13.3333px\">dur_TVIGday_min</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13.3333px\"><font color=\"#000000\">) for MVPA, I found the time spent in MVPA is much higher than the &quot;file summary reports&quot; MVPA value. Please see the attached files. Thanks for helping.</font></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13.3333px\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13.3333px\"><font color=\"#000000\">Wenxi</font></span></div></div>"
